*** Settings ***
Documentation       Business actions for the accessibility checks - these keywords are used in tests.
Resource            ${EXECDIR}/resources/interactions/browser_interactions.resource
Resource            ${EXECDIR}/resources/interactions/accessibility_interactions.resource


*** Keywords ***
Start Audit Browser
    [Documentation]    Starts the browser for the checks.
    Launch Browser

Stop Audit Browser
    [Documentation]    Closes the browser.
    Close All Web Browsers

Audit Accessibility Of Page
    [Documentation]    Opens a page, checks it with axe-core, automatically writes an HTML report to
    ...    results/accessibility/ (linked in the log) and returns the violations found.
    [Arguments]    ${address}
    Go To Address    ${address}
    ${violations}    Audit Accessibility Of Current Page
    RETURN    ${violations}

Audit Accessibility Of Current Page
    [Documentation]    Checks the page that is open right now (e.g. after login) and writes the report.
    ${address}    Read Current Address
    ${violations}    Find Accessibility Violations
    ${report}    Write Accessibility Report    ${address}    ${violations}
    Log    <a href="${report}">Accessibility report for ${address}</a>    html=True
    RETURN    ${violations}

Log In For Audit
    [Documentation]    Logs in with the credentials of the active environment (login page from login_page).
    Go To Address    ${WEB_BASE_URL}
    Fill Field    ${LOGIN_USERNAME_FIELD}    ${LOGINS}[${ENV}][username]
    Fill Secret Field    ${LOGIN_PASSWORD_FIELD}    ${LOGINS}[${ENV}][password]
    Click On    ${LOGIN_BUTTON}
    Wait For Visible Element    ${MAIN_TITLE}

Open Cart For Audit
    [Documentation]    Opens the cart so that it can be checked.
    Click On    ${MAIN_CART_LINK}
    Wait For Visible Element    ${CART_TITLE}
